{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuijTjMvYK7wKSY4BFPg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Miniflare now serves its local testing endpoints under the **`/cdn-cgi/mf/`** prefix. To fire the local scheduled trigger, send a request to `/cdn-cgi/mf/scheduled`, for example `curl \"http://localhost:8787/cdn-cgi/mf/scheduled?cron=*+*+*+*+*\"`. You can add the optional `time` and `cron` query parameters to set the event's values. In older Miniflare versions this was `/.mf/scheduled`, which is from memory; I didn't check it here.\n\nCloudflare's general Workers docs (for `wrangler dev`) give a different path: `/cdn-cgi/handler/scheduled`, with an optional `?format=json`. If you're using Miniflare directly instead of through Wrangler, you can also call `(await mf.getWorker()).scheduled({ scheduledTime, cron })` from code instead of using HTTP.\n\nSources:\n- [Miniflare – Scheduled Events](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/miniflare/core/scheduled/)\n- [Workers – Scheduled handler](https://docs-durable-objects-instance-replaced-errors.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/handlers/scheduled/index.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":22492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1382},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52961496-1bba-477c-872e-23c64e8e990c","uuid":"bce492fa-30a1-4c30-89fa-2d41a9f0be1c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:13:40.669Z","request_id":"req_011CfuijTVDzJyCDgBiXQwgk"}
